@startuml cls-attendance-biometric
title Class Diagram — Attendance & Biometric

skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
hide circle

class ClassSession <<external — scheduling>> {
}
class AcademicActor <<external — academic>> {
}
class School <<external — academic>> {
}
class Cohort <<external — academic>> {
}
class Person <<external — identity>> {
}
class AppUser <<external — identity>> {
}

enum AttendanceStatus <<enumeration>> {
  Present
  Absent
  Late
  Justified
}

enum CaptureMethod <<enumeration>> {
  FACIAL
  MANUAL
  IOT
  IMPORT
}

enum ReviewStatus <<enumeration>> {
  Pending
  Approved
  Rejected
}

enum BiometricType <<enumeration>> {
  FACIAL
  FINGERPRINT
}

enum UpdateStatus <<enumeration>> {
  Pending
  In_Review
  Approved
  Rejected
}

class AttendanceRecord {
  +attendanceRecordId: Long
  +classSessionId: Long
  +academicActorId: Long
  +attendanceStatus: AttendanceStatus
  +capturedAt: DateTime
  +captureMethod: CaptureMethod
  +matchScore: Decimal
  +record()
}

class JustificationType {
  +justificationTypeId: Int
  +schoolId: Int
  +name: String
  +description: String
  +requiresAttachment: Boolean
  +status: Boolean
}

class Justification {
  +justificationId: Long
  +attendanceRecordId: Long
  +justificationTypeId: Int
  +reason: String
  +submittedAt: DateTime
  +reviewedBy: UUID
  +reviewedAt: DateTime
  +reviewStatus: ReviewStatus
  +resolutionNotes: String
  +submit()
  +review(decision)
}

class SupportingDocument {
  +supportingDocumentId: Long
  +justificationId: Long
  +fileName: String
  +storageUri: String
  +mimeType: String
  +sizeBytes: Long
  +upload()
}

class AttendanceReport <<derived projection, no FKs>> {
  +reportId: UUID
  +schoolId: Int
  +cohortId: Long
  +generatedBy: UUID
  +reportType: String
  +filters: JSON
  +result: JSON
  +generatedAt: DateTime
}

class BiometricUpdateCase {
  +caseId: UUID
  +personId: UUID
  +biometricType: BiometricType
  +fingerNumber: Int
  +currentEmbeddingRef: String
  +reason: String
  +updateStatus: UpdateStatus
  +requestedBy: UUID
  +requestedAt: DateTime
  +reviewedBy: UUID
  +reviewedAt: DateTime
  +resolutionNotes: String
  +request()
  +review(decision)
}

class FacialEmbedding <<MongoDB document>> {
  +_id: ObjectId
  +personId: UUID
  +templateVersion: Int
  +encoding: Float[]
  +modelVersion: String
  +enrolledAt: DateTime
  +isActive: Boolean
  +enroll()
  +deactivate()
}

class FingerprintEmbedding <<MongoDB document>> {
  +_id: ObjectId
  +personId: UUID
  +fingerNumber: Int
  +templateVersion: Int
  +encoding: Float[]
  +modelVersion: String
  +enrolledAt: DateTime
  +isActive: Boolean
  +enroll()
  +deactivate()
}

AttendanceRecord "1" -- "0..1" Justification : justification.attendance_record_id FK\nUNIQUE one-to-one
JustificationType "1" -- "0..*" Justification : justification.justification_type_id FK
Justification "1" -- "0..*" SupportingDocument : supporting_document.justification_id FK
AttendanceRecord --> AttendanceStatus
AttendanceRecord --> CaptureMethod
Justification --> ReviewStatus
BiometricUpdateCase --> BiometricType
BiometricUpdateCase --> UpdateStatus

AttendanceRecord ..> ClassSession : class_session_id\n(cross-context, no FK)
AttendanceRecord ..> AcademicActor : academic_actor_id\n(cross-context, no FK)
Justification ..> AppUser : reviewed_by\n(cross-context, no FK)
AttendanceReport ..> School : school_id\n(no FK, derived projection)
AttendanceReport ..> Cohort : cohort_id\n(no FK, derived projection)
AttendanceReport ..> AppUser : generated_by\n(no FK, derived projection)
BiometricUpdateCase ..> Person : person_id\n(cross-context, no FK)
BiometricUpdateCase ..> AppUser : requested_by / reviewed_by\n(cross-context, no FK)
BiometricUpdateCase ..> FacialEmbedding : current_embedding_ref\n(cross-paradigm Mongo _id, no FK)
BiometricUpdateCase ..> FingerprintEmbedding : current_embedding_ref\n(cross-paradigm Mongo _id, no FK)
FacialEmbedding ..> Person : person_id\n(cross-context, no FK)
FingerprintEmbedding ..> Person : person_id\n(cross-context, no FK)

note right of AttendanceRecord
  RN-22: one record per academic_actor per
  class_session (uq_attendance_session_actor).
  RN-23: the session must be Open when
  recorded. Only captureMethod=MANUAL is wired
  for the alternative path (RN-26) — FACIAL
  capture is designed but no client calls the
  write yet, see SEQ-01.
end note

note left of JustificationType
  school_id NULL = global type.
  uq_justification_type_school_name plus a
  partial unique on name WHERE school_id IS NULL.
end note

note right of Justification
  RN-32: exactly one justification per
  attendance_record (1:1, UNIQUE). RN-33
  (intended): requires_attachment should block
  approval without a document — not enforced
  server-side today. RN-36 (intended): approval
  should cascade attendance_status to Justified
  — it does not (see ST-02 / SEQ-03).
end note

note bottom of SupportingDocument
  Designed but not wired: no client ever calls
  this endpoint with a real file, see SEQ-03.
end note

note left of BiometricUpdateCase
  Logically owned by Biometric, physically
  hosted in the configuration schema (transient,
  see AGENTS.md §4.6). chk_finger_number: 1..10
  only if biometricType=FINGERPRINT, else NULL.
  requestedBy/requestedAt are mandatory. This is
  the canonical shape — ms-biometric also runs
  its own independent MongoDB implementation of
  the same feature with no requestedBy, no
  fingerNumber check, and no sync to this one.
  See SEQ-04.
end note

note right of FacialEmbedding
  RN-28: only one active embedding per person
  at a time (isActive flag) — enroll()
  deactivates the previous template.
end note

note as N1
  All SQL classes also carry the standard audit
  block (created_at/updated_at/deleted_at/
  created_by/updated_by/deleted_by/row_version)
  — omitted here for readability. See
  AGENTS.md §2.2 and 06-data/domains/
  05-attendance.md / 06-biometric.md for the
  column-level ER view. The two MongoDB
  collections have no FKs by nature
  (cross-paradigm).
end note

@enduml
